# Mia's in-RAM reasoning memory (patch 0036's KeptReasoning, adapted from jayleaton's 0620) cut out. It kept the
# reasoning text of tool-calling replies in RAM (1,024 replies or 32 MiB, emptied at every restart) and put it back into
# later requests whose client dropped it, found by the server's call ids or by a signature of the conversation's roles,
# texts and calls. Turn records (9004/9005) do that job with the prompt state itself: the exact tokens, thinking
# included, saved, read back and evicted with the state, after restarts too, and for every reply, not only tool calls.
# The memory was a second cache with a retention of its own, and its signature ignored pictures: the same words with
# another picture got the first conversation's thinking (checked on the CPU, 2026-10-08). Reasoning a client dropped now
# comes back only through a record. mgllm, 2026-10-08.
# Tests: tests/test_9007_no_kept_reasoning.py (CPU; needs TF_GLM_TEST_MODEL_DIR).

